Z||000000||chris6878||09-21-1999||10:29 PM||||My Car just recently went crazy...<BR>I was heading home 2 nights ago.. and i hear a loud noise in the engine area... I thought the engine threw a rod.. i was near home when this happened.. i turned of the engine and coasted into my drive way...   <P>I checked my flywheel and Torque Converter.. (these came loose before) and they were fine.<BR>I took the valve cover off and started the engine and something isnt right in the top off the motor, it makes a loud rattling noise..      Oh yeah..  my #1 spark plug's gap was smashed... what could have possiblly hit the spark plug...   i am thinking warped valve or something or maybe lifters causing the noise...????  it has ran fine with no problems until now... and the engine was rebuilt about 8 months ago...  I found a complete 84 that has been wrecked  with good motor and tranny and i  can get it for 100 dollars... might just change them out...  any suggestions..???? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||JetroGT||09-22-1999||12:16 AM||||Mybe you lost a few teeth on your cam gear. Usually it will make that clasic ticking noise found on most high miles 2.5 GM 4 cyls.<BR>Then after a few months to a few years the teeth will be compleatly striped off and then you get a new engine. The gear is not metal. GM used the non metal gear to make the car a little more quite.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dale||09-22-1999||02:27 AM||||If your spark plug gap was smashed you sucked something up (not good).  Do you have any compresion in that cyl?||||reg||1
